          "document_id": "55014240-5eaa-4cde-86bb-08acf68de201",
          "end_char": 9557,
          "exact_text": "The First Consul has special duties and prerogative in which he is temporarily replaced by one of his colleagues, when there is need.",
          "quote_hash": "968fc7721ac7132471f17d28ae322e1f4b4a7d66cebe48a58de8d729b123199f",
          "start_char": 9424
        }
      ],
      "text": "The Constitution establishes a formal legal framework for the change of authority, detailing institutional roles and procedures."
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "finding:1:clause:0",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "application_id": "0f22c327-96a1-4b69-9d7c-766ef884f97a",
          "code_id": "GOVERNMENT_STRUCTURE",
          "document_id": "55014240-5eaa-4cde-86bb-08acf68de201",
          "end_char": 4670,
          "exact_text": "The other two consuls, during the month following the expiration of their duties, can take seats in the Senate, but they are not required to make use of this right.",
          "quote_hash": "d318fdf1e86c0bc2f29cf4c7c5e7d8ef98491496af599dfc36d6a97871060ba8",
          "start_char": 4506
        }
      ],
      "text": "The memoir portrays the change of authority as resulting from personal interactions and secret negotiations."
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "finding:2:clause:0",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "application_id": "711190fe-d475-4e45-916d-452dc45df47e",
